  "id": "a79fe637-10bd-561d-b9a8-ac91ab5f9673",
  "slug": "red-velvet-pots-de-creme-recipe-8781823",
  "name": "Red Velvet Pots de Cr\u00e8me",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "These red velvet pots de cr\u00e8me are a special occasion chocolate dessert that is plenty decadent, but still somehow light. With a deeper chocolate flavor than typical red velvet cake, and a little bit of cream cheese tanginess. they are super easy, gorgeous, and incredibly delicious.",
  "cuisine": "French",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "For pots de cr\u00e8me, whisk together milk, cream, and egg yolks in a saucepan. Cook, stirring constantly with a spatula over medium heat, until the mixture is hot and steamy, but has not begun to simmer yet. An instant read thermometer inserted into the mixture should read 160 degrees F (71 degrees C)."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Remove from heat, add chocolate, and swirl pan a few times to settle chocolate down. Let sit for 2 minutes. Add salt, vanilla, and red coloring."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "After 2 minutes, add cream cheese, and whisk everything until smooth. If cream cheese is not mixing in completely, use a stick blender to mix for a few seconds."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Transfer mixture into serving glasses or jars. Place jars on a tray and tap each one gently a few times to bring any air bubbles to the surface. Cover with plastic wrap and chill in the refrigerator until cold and firm, at least 2 hours or up to overnight."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "For whipped topping, add heavy cream, confectioner\u2019s sugar, cream cheese, and vanilla to a bowl, and whisk until medium-stiff peaks form. Add to a piping bag, and pipe (or spoon) over chilled pots de cr\u00e8me. Dust lightly with cocoa powder, and serve."
    }
  ],
  "servings": 4,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 5,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 25,
  "rest_time_minutes": null,
  "difficulty": "medium",
